1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,800
Hi, we're Hyeonmin and Jaewu, and this is DropPDF.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:07,200
It turns your files into PDFs,

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:10,600
and turns PDFs back into Word or PowerPoint, all right in your browser.

4
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:14,800
There's nothing to install, and your files never leave your computer.

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:19,600
Let's start by dragging in a few files: a Word report, an Excel sheet,

6
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:23,000
a ZIP full of trip photos, and a PDF brochure.

7
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:26,200
Each row shows what the file will turn into.

8
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:30,300
Since the brochure is already a PDF, I get to choose what it becomes:

9
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:34,000
Word, PowerPoint, images, or plain text.

10
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:37,000
If I only need one file, I just click Convert on that row.

11
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:39,300
In a moment, the report is saved,

12
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:44,000
and here's the PDF it made,

13
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:48,800
with the table and layout just like the original.

14
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:52,000
For everything else, I click Convert all.

15
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:55,300
My favorite part is the photo ZIP.

16
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:59,500
Instead of four separate files, DropPDF puts every photo into one PDF,

17
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:04,800
one page per photo, in the right order.

18
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:08,500
The brochure is now a Word document.

19
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:15,200
Here's a quick preview in the Library,

20
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:17,800
and here it is open in Microsoft Word.

21
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:20,400
It's not just a picture of the page.

22
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:23,800
I can click into the heading and keep typing,

23
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:27,300
while the photos and background stay right where they were.

24
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:30,000
The same brochure can also become slides.

25
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:33,500
I just switch the format to PowerPoint and hit Convert again,

26
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:36,800
with no need to upload anything twice.

27
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:41,400
And here's the brochure as a PowerPoint slide.

28
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:44,600
Every result is saved in the Library, so it's still here even after I close the browser.

29
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:47,500
I can search to find a file quickly,

30
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:53,500
open a preview without downloading it,

31
00:01:53,600 --> 00:02:00,500
and rename a file or add a memo so I remember what it's for.

32
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:04,400
If I need another format later, Convert again sends the original back to the list,

33
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:08,100
so I don't have to dig it up again.

34
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:11,800
Anything I don't need is one click to delete,

35
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:15,400
and Delete all clears the whole library.

36
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:21,000
So that's DropPDF: drop in your files, pick a format,

37
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:25,400
and keep everything organized in one place.

38
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:28,600
We hope it saves you some time.

39
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:32,300
Thanks for watching!

